{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-03-05","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-03-05","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-03-05","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1873","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"P000613","fullName":"Rep. Panetta, Jimmy [D-CA-19]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"D000230","fullName":"Rep. Davis, Donald G. [D-NC-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-03-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"C001103","fullName":"Rep. Carter, Earl L. \"Buddy\" [R-GA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"A000372","fullName":"Rep. Allen, Rick W. [R-GA-12]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"J000301","fullName":"Rep. Johnson, Dusty [R-SD-At Large]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SD"},{"bioguideId":"C001059","fullName":"Rep. Costa, Jim [D-CA-21]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"Y000067","fullName":"Rep. Yakym, Rudy [R-IN-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"S001228","fullName":"Rep. Schmidt, Derek [R-KS-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-06-25","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KS"},{"bioguideId":"R000603","fullName":"Rep. Rouzer, David [R-NC-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-08-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"F000446","fullName":"Rep. Feenstra, Randy [R-IA-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"S001225","fullName":"Rep. Sorensen, Eric [D-IL-17]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"B001295","fullName":"Rep. Bost, Mike [R-IL-12]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"W000831","fullName":"Rep. Walkinshaw, James R. [D-VA-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"M001227","fullName":"Rep. McClellan, Jennifer L. [D-VA-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"V000138","fullName":"Rep. Vindman, Eugene Simon [D-VA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-07-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:11:52+00:00","id":"hr1873-119","introducedDate":"2025-03-05","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-05","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"laws":[],"number":"1873","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Taxation","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"K000376","district":16,"fullName":"Rep. Kelly, Mike [R-PA-16]","party":"R","state":"PA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-03-05","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Broadband Grant Tax Treatment Act</strong></p><p>This bill excludes from gross income (for federal tax purposes) certain grants received for broadband deployment.</p><p>As background, contributions of capital to a corporation generally are not taxable income. However, under an exception enacted in 2017 by the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, grants from a government or civic organization are not contributions to capital and, thus, treated as taxable income. Prior to the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act, the&nbsp;Internal Revenue Service (IRS) considered certain grants from a government or civic organization&nbsp;contributions of capital and, thus, not taxable income.</p><p>The bill specifically excludes from gross income grants received for broadband deployment from the</p><ul><li>National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) Broadband Equity, Access, and Deployment Program;</li><li>NTIA State Digital Equity Capacity Grant Program;</li><li>NTIA Digital Equity Competitive Grant Program;</li><li>NTIA Enabling Middle Mile Broadband Infrastructure Program;</li><li>Department of Agriculture ReConnect Program;</li><li>Coronavirus State and Local&nbsp;Fiscal Recovery Funds&nbsp;and the Coronavirus Capital Projects Fund; and</li><li>NTIA Tribal Broadband Connectivity Program and the Broadband Infrastructure Program.</li></ul><p>The bill also requires the IRS to issue guidance on the exclusion from gross income of such grants.</p><p>The bill applies to funds received in tax years ending after March 11, 2023.</p>","updateDate":"2026-01-26T15:17:37Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Broadband Grant Tax Treatment Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:32:21Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:32:21Z"}
